    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="0563" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221 Dahl, Harold/68: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vigo</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Graves</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vigo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-27T19:00:00+01:00">September 27, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 30, 5 p.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d541-f1"/> I am informed from Salamanca
                    that Harold Dahl is to be tried by court martial at 11:00 o’clock on the morning
                    of October 5. The assistant judge in charge of the case, who was apparently the
                    person telephoning me, asked that I attend the trial. <pb facs="0564" n="552"
                        xml:id="pg552"/> He appeared particularly interested due to the foreign
                    correspondents at Salamanca who will cover the case. I told him, however, that I
                    was not planning to attend the trial. Repeated to Seville.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Graves</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d541-f1" n="6" xml:id="d541-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it instructed the Consul not to attend the court martial of Harold
                    Dahl (852.2221 Dahl, Harold/15).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
